==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|bine|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|bini|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{recons|biniz|lang=gem-pro}}, representing an ''-n-'' variant of Germanic {{recons|bijō|lang=gem-pro}}.  Compare Upper German [[Beie]]. Cognate with {{etyl|bay|-}} {{term|Bein||bee|lang=bay}}, {{etyl|osx|-}} {{term|bini|lang=osx}}.

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f||Bienen}}

# [[bee]]
# cute, sexy woman

